<styles>
<s type="P" name="Normal" followedby="Current Settings" props="font-family:Tinos; margin-top:0pt; color:000000; margin-left:0pt; text-position:normal; widows:2; font-style:normal; text-indent:0in; font-variant:normal; font-weight:normal; margin-right:0pt; font-size:12pt; text-decoration:none; margin-bottom:0pt; line-height:1.0; bgcolor:transparent; text-align:left; font-stretch:normal"/>
</styles>
<pagesize pagetype="A4" orientation="portrait" width="210.000000" height="297.000000" units="mm" page-scale="1.000000"/>
<section xid="3">
<p style="Normal" xid="4" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt">TASK 2:</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="5"><c props="font-size:20pt"></c><c props="font-size:20pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="6" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt">The sampling is not quite uniform. The first node is chosen at random, then a random neighbor of</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="7" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt">that node is chosen, so more popular nodes have a higher chance at being picked since they are</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="8" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt">more likely to be someone's neighbor. 83% of the edges are positive and roughly 17% are negative.</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="9" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt">The structural balance seems to hold for this network since almost all of the sampled triangles</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="10" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt">are strongly balanced.</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="45" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt"></c><c props="font-size:20pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="46" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt">Task 2</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="47" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt"></c><c props="font-size:20pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="48" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt">The triangles are sampled by randomly selecting a node and then choosing two of its neighbors. This sampling method introduces bias because the probability of selecting a particular triangle is influenced by the degree distribution of nodes in the network. Nodes with high degree are more likely to be selected</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="49" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt"></c><c props="font-size:20pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="50" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt">tot number edges = 711210 tot number pos edges = 589888/711210 = 83% to number neg edges = 118619/711210 = 17%</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="51" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt"></c><c props="font-size:20pt"></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="52" props="text-align:left; dom-dir:ltr"><c props="font-size:20pt">yes i would say so, only one triangle was unbalanced</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="11"><c></c></p>
</section>
</abiword>
